COMMAND NAME: mppsizecalc.sh

Shows the disk space usage for a given database, table, or index.

*****************************************************
SYNOPSIS
*****************************************************

mppsizecalc.sh {-x <database_name> [-p | -m] | {-t <schema>.<table_name> [-h] 
               [-i] [-a <database_name>]}} [-B <parallel_processes>] 
               [-d <data_directory>] [-s b|k|m|g] [-f] [-l <logfile_directory>] 
               [-D] [-q] [-? | -v]


*****************************************************
DESCRIPTION
*****************************************************

The mppsizecalc.sh script can be used to determine the disk space usage for a 
Greenplum database, table, or index. mppsizecalc.sh displays the following 
information:

* The total disk space usage for a specified database (mirrors and primary 
  combined).

* The primary disk space usage for a specified table. Note that for 
  partitioned parent tables, you must use the -h option to inquire about 
  child tables.

* The primary disk space usage for a specified table index.

* The disk usage per active segment (if -f option is supplied).

If checking disk space usage on a specific table or index, sizing information 
is shown for active (primary) segments only. If checking size of a database, 
total sizing is shown by default (primary and mirror).


*****************************************************
OPTIONS
*****************************************************

-x <database_name>

Either a database name or a table name is required. The database for which 
you want to see the total disk space usage (primary and mirror segments).


-p (primary segments only)

Obtain database sizing information for primary segments only. The default 
is to show total disk space usage for databases (including mirrors) and to 
show primary disk space usage only for tables and indexes.


-m (mirror segments only)

Obtain database sizing information for mirror segments only. The default is 
to show total disk space usage for databases (including mirrors) and to show 
primary disk space usage only for tables and indexes.


-t <schema>.<table_name>

Either a database name or a table name is required. The schema qualified 
table name for which you want to see the disk space usage. For a table, disk 
space usage is shown for active segments only by default. 


-h (show child table hierarchy)

Optional. If the table supplied with the -t option has child tables associated 
with it, this option will show information for the inherited child tables as 
well.


-i (show index size)

Optional. Shows the index size for the named table.


-a <database_name_for_table>

Optional. The name of the database for the specified table. If not supplied, 
the script uses the default database (which is the most recently created 
database).


-B <parallel_processes>

The number of segments to check in parallel. If not specified, the script 
will start up to 60 parallel processes depending on how many segment instances 
for which it needs to check sizing information.


-d <master_data_directory>

Optional. The master host data directory. If not specified, the value set for 
$MASTER_DATA_DIRECTORY will be used.


-s b | k | m| g (bytes, kilobytes, megabytes, or gigabytes)

Optional. Display disk usage size information in bytes (b), kilobytes (k), 
megabytes (m) or gigabytes (g). The default is kilobytes (k).


-f (per segment results)

Optional. Displays the disk space usage per active segment. The default is 
to show total disk space usage for all segments.


-l <logfile_directory>

The directory to write the log file. Defaults to ~/gpAdminLogs.


-D (show detailed output)

Optional. If supplied will output all script log messages to the screen.


-q (no screen output)

Run in quiet mode. Command output is not displayed on the screen, but is still 
written to the log file.


-? (help)

Displays the online help.


-v (show script version)

Displays the version, status, last updated date, and check sum of this script.


*****************************************************
EXAMPLES
*****************************************************

Show the total disk space usage for a table:

mppsizecalc.sh -t products


Show the total disk space usage for a database. Show size in megabytes 
rather than kilobytes:

mppsizecalc.sh -x gpdb -s m


Show the disk space usage per segment for a partitioned table:

mppsizecalc.sh -t products -h -f


Show the disk space usage per segment for a database:

mppsizecalc.sh -x gpdb -f


Show the index sizes for a table that is in another database besides the 
default:

mppsizecalc.sh -t products -a gpdb2 -i


